{"archetypes":[{"name":"variable-scope","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Plan names shell variables ($TOOL_TAG, $REPO_ROOT, $MANIFEST_RAW_PATH, $STATUS, $TMPDIR_ARG, $SPAWN_BRANCH) inside emit_manifest_invalid_or_recover without verifying their in-scope names against the actual dispatcher script; wrong names silently produce empty values under set -e with || true guards.","prompt_body":"Read skills/implement/scripts/step2-implement.sh and identify every shell variable the plan expects to be in scope inside the new emit_manifest_invalid_or_recover function: specifically $TOOL_TAG, $REPO_ROOT, $MANIFEST_RAW_PATH, $STATUS, $TMPDIR_ARG, and $SPAWN_BRANCH. For each variable, verify it is declared, exported, or assigned before the call sites the plan targets at lines 486, 490, 507, and 548. Flag any variable the plan names that does not appear in the script under that name, any that is local to a subshell or conditional branch making it unavailable at those call sites, and any where the plan's FINDING_1 correction (TOOL_LABEL to TOOL_TAG) may have missed a second wrong alias. Also check that emit_manifest_invalid_or_recover's exit 0 cannot fall through to the forbidden-emit sites the plan cites at lines 262/841/850/867. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"predicate-parity","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan's inline jq self-validation predicate claims to mirror the dispatcher's complete-branch predicate at step2-implement.sh:496-508 including summary_bullets length bounds (>=1 and <=5) that may not match the actual dispatcher, creating a gap where implementers pass the prompt check but fail dispatcher validation.","prompt_body":"Read skills/implement/scripts/step2-implement.sh lines 486-560 and extract the exact jq predicate(s) used for manifest validation on the complete branch. Compare field-by-field against the plan's proposed inline jq block for the Self-validate before atomic rename section: check schema_version, status values, commit_message type and length, files_touched array and object and path, summary_bullets type and length bounds (the plan states >=1 and <=5 — confirm the dispatcher uses identical bounds), tests_added_or_modified, todos_left, oos_observations, and the needs_qa and bailed branches. Also read skills/implement/references/codex-manifest-schema.md and verify the plan's JSON template includes all fields listed there with correct types. Flag any field the prompt predicate checks that the dispatcher does not (over-validation causing false failures) and any the dispatcher checks that the prompt predicate omits (under-validation defeating the prevention goal). Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"baseline-snapshot","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The recovery gate's porcelain-delta check requires a new step2-prelaunch-porcelain.txt file the plan places only vaguely 'at the top of the cursor/codex launch path' without confirming both tool branches are covered or how tests M2/M7/M8/M9/M10 seed this file in their scratch repos.","prompt_body":"Read skills/implement/scripts/step2-implement.sh and locate where the existing pre-launch snapshot (step2-baseline.txt or equivalent) is written; identify whether separate cursor and codex launch code paths exist and whether a single baseline write covers both. Then read skills/implement/scripts/test-step2-dispatch.sh to understand how the existing harness creates scratch repos and seeds baseline files, and assess whether Tests M2 (empty tree), M7 (untracked-only), M8 (protected-path delta), M9 (submodule delta), and M10 (branch-changed) can be correctly exercised without each test explicitly writing a step2-prelaunch-porcelain.txt to the scratch tmpdir. Flag any gap where the plan places the baseline write without identifying the exact code location, where a test fixture omits the required file, or where the delta between pre-launch and post-launch porcelain output could include manifest.json itself (contaminating the non-empty-delta gate). Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
